BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Atlantis reentry scenario 2</h1>
<p>Partway through entry, the Orbiter is rolled to point the lift vector to the right to curve the trajectory towards the Cape.

As your trajectory moves, you will eventually need to S-turn a few times to avoid overshooting and ending up too far from the runway to glide to it.
You also should keep AOA above 30 degrees, as per real life structural/thermal limits. 
Thus, to avoid lift making you skip out of the atmosphere, you need to bank from side to side to limit the vertical lift component.
</p>
END_HYPERDESC

